# Line endings.
#
# core.autocrlf is enabled on this machine, which would rewrite LF -> CRLF on
# checkout. That breaks two things here:
#
#   * `gradlew` is a POSIX shell script (#!/bin/sh). With CRLF the kernel cannot
#     parse the shebang and `./gradlew` fails on Linux/macOS with
#     "bad interpreter: No such file or directory".
#   * JSON, lang files and Java sources are compared byte-wise by the build and
#     by the verifier; mixed endings make diffs unreadable.
#
# Everything is therefore stored and checked out with LF.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Shell / Gradle wrappers must stay LF, explicitly.
gradlew text eol=lf
*.sh text eol=lf

# Windows batch files need CRLF to run.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary assets: never touch.
*.png binary
*.jar binary
*.nbt binary
*.zip binary

# Generated data is diff-heavy; mark it so review stays readable.
src/generated/resources/** linguist-generated=true
